# How to use this lesson

W[J] generates connected diagrams. Its Legendre transform Γ[φ_cl] generates one-particle-irreducible diagrams. The classical field φ_cl=δW/δJ satisfies δΓ/δφ_cl=−J, the quantum-corrected equation of motion. Lesson 67's resummed propagator is the inverse of Γ's second derivative. Expect five to seven hours.

## Learning objectives

- Define Γ[φ_cl]=W[J]−∫J φ_cl with φ_cl=δW/δJ.

- Invert the relation to δΓ/δφ_cl=−J.

- State that the vertices of Γ are 1PI correlators.

- Identify Γ''(φ_cl) as the inverse of the full connected two-point function.

