# 1 The Legendre transform

Lesson 80 gave φ_cl(x)≡⟨φ(x)⟩_J=δW/δJ(x). Invert this, treating J as a functional of φ_cl, and define

$$ Γ[φ_cl] = W[J] − ∫ d⁴x J(x) φ_cl(x)

Differentiating with respect to φ_cl, the terms in which J varies cancel by the inverse-function theorem, leaving

$$ δΓ / δφ_cl(x) = − J(x)

At J=0, the physical vacuum, δΓ/δφ_cl=0: the effective action is stationary at the true mean field. That is the quantum Euler–Lagrange equation.

### Worked example 1

In a free theory W=½∫J Δ J and φ_cl=Δ J, so J=Δ⁻¹ φ_cl and Γ=½∫J Δ J−∫J φ_cl=−½∫φ_cl Δ⁻¹ φ_cl. Thus Γ_free is the original classical action (up to the sign conventions of iS), with no loops, as expected: a free theory has no 1PI loop vertices.

# 2 One-particle irreducibility

A connected diagram may fall into two pieces if a single propagator is cut. The 1PI diagrams are those that do not. Vertices of Γ are 1PI because the Legendre transform strips the full external propagators: it is the inverse of W's second derivative at two points, and it amputates one-particle reducible chains at n points. Tree diagrams built from Γ vertices, with Γ'' as the internal propagator, then reproduce all connected correlators of W. In slogans: trees in Γ equal loops in the original theory, provided only 1PI blobs are used as vertices.

# 3 The inverse propagator

Differentiating δΓ/δφ=−J once more,

$$ ∫ d⁴y  (δ²Γ / δφ_cl(x) δφ_cl(y))  (δ²W / δJ(y) δJ(z)) = − δ⁴(x−z)

so Γ'' is minus the inverse of W''. But W'' is the connected two-point function, i.e. the full propagator S_F′ of Lesson 67. Mass renormalization is the statement that Γ'' has a zero at the physical p̸=m. Charge renormalization is a statement about the three-point 1PI vertex in Γ at vanishing photon momentum.

### Worked example 2

Where did Lesson 67's geometric series of self-energy insertions go? It is the expansion of (Γ''_free − Σ)⁻¹, which is exactly inverting Γ''=Γ''_free−Σ. The effective action packages the resummation as “use the inverted second derivative.”

# 4 What Γ does not skip

Writing Γ does not remove the need to regularize (Lesson 66) or to absorb parameters (Lesson 67). It reorganizes the same loops. Its gift is vocabulary: “the quantum equation of motion” and “1PI” become derivatives of one object.

